00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
You'll laugh again! You'll cry again!! You'll hurl again!!!

2
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Wayne's World 2 is a comedy, music film directed by Stephen Surjik.

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
A message from Jim Morrison in a dream prompts cable access TV stars Wayne and Garth
to put on a rock concert, "Waynestock," with Aerosmith as headliners.

4
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
But amid the preparations, Wayne frets that a record producer is putting the moves on his
girlfriend, Cassandra, while Garth handles the advances of mega-babe Honey Hornée.

5
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Wayne Campbell, played by Mike Myers.

6
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Garth Algar, played by Dana Carvey.

7
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Bobby Cahn, played by Christopher Walken.

8
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Cassandra Wong, played by Tia Carrere.

9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Milton, played by Chris Farley.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Jeff Wong, played by James Hong.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Wayne's World 2 is a 1993 American comedy film directed by Stephen Surjik and starring Mike Myers and Dana
Carvey as hosts of a public-access television cable television show in Aurora, Illinois.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film is the sequel to Wayne's World (1992), which was itself
adapted from a sketch on NBC's Saturday Night Live.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film explores themes of concert, rock 'n' roll,
dreams, love of one's life, talk show.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The tone is lighthearted.
